    "title": "Concept: What is a Community?",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">A <strong>community</strong> in biology is made up of all the different species or populations that live together in the same habitat. These species interact with each other and share resources. For example, a pond community includes species like fish, frogs, insects, algae, and aquatic plants.</p>",
