    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">In a community, organisms interact with both biotic and abiotic factors. For example, plants depend on abiotic factors like sunlight and soil minerals, and on biotic factors like insects for pollination. Animals depend on abiotic factors such as water and temperature, and on biotic factors such as food and predator presence.</p>",
